Work is complete. Summary of what this run did:

**Reproduced** the phase's original finding and confirmed the previous attempt's seeded SplitMix64 generator was in place and green.

**Found and fixed a real defect the previous attempt missed.** `random_int` scaled the raw width when a bound was fractional, so `random(0, 100.5)` answered `100.5` at seed 581 (and could answer `101`, outside the range) — 26 of 3000 seeds were fractions, from a builtin whose own passing test asserts `value.fract() == 0.0`. `random(0.2, 0.8)`, a range holding no integer, answered `0.2`. The existing tests missed it because they only ever drew from integer bounds, so the buggy branch was never taken.

The fix counts the range's actual members, `ceil(min)..=floor(max)`, and refuses a range holding no whole number by name.

**Added one failing test first**, watched it fail on exactly that assertion, then made it green. It sweeps 3000 seeds across four fractional-ended ranges.

**Gates:**

| Gate | Result |
|---|---|
| `cargo fmt --all -- --check` | pass |
| `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` | pass, 0 warnings, no `allow` added |
| `cargo test --all-targets` | 1121 passed, 0 failed, 0 ignored (41 binaries) |
| `./rbops/verify.sh phase-037` | **not run — `rbops/` does not exist in this checkout** |

I re-verified every Definition-of-Done claim against the rebuilt binary rather than trusting the prior report, including the two-process determinism diff (empty, exit 0, both seeded and unseeded), `non-permutations=0 identity=0` across 100 separate processes, and the 91-distinct draw count.

Two DoD lines remain arithmetically unsatisfiable — `random_number(0, 100)` producing ≤101 distinct values in 200 draws, and a 400–600 per-bucket band over 1000 draws in ten buckets. Both are reported in REPORT.md and FINDINGS.md with the arithmetic; no test was weakened to make either look satisfied.

`REPORT.md` and `FINDINGS.md` are rewritten with verified claims, including a new FINDINGS entry on why the resumed phase reported complete while carrying an uncovered broken branch.

DONE
